<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · river</p><h1 class="enc-title">Oder River</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Oder is a river of central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a> flowing north through present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/czech-republic">Czechia</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> into the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baltic-sea">Baltic Sea</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a> secured its mouth in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pomerania">Pomerania</a> during <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thirty-tyrants">the Thirty</a> Years' War in the 1630s. Control of the Oder estuary was part of the Baltic dominion on which the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/swedish-empire">Swedish Empire</a> was built.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/oder-river.jpg" alt="Oder River" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Grzegorz Kilian · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:WyspaRedzinska-GK.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
